        "problem": "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\left(1+\\dfrac{1}{n}\\right)^{3n}}.$",
        "worked_solution": "Recall the following special limit: \n\n$$\ne = \\lim_{n \\to  \\infty} \\left(1+\\dfrac{1}{n}\\right)^{n}\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite the given limit using the algebra of limits, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{1}{n})}^{3n} & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{[{(1+\\frac{1}{n})}^{n}]}^{3} \\\\  & ={[{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{1}{n})}^{n}]}^{3} \\\\  & ={e}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
